{"id": "EUVD-2026-102272", "enisaUuid": "4705733a-357d-359c-b075-8905cd39a043", "description": "ytnef through 2.1.2 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in DecompressRTF() in lib/ytnef.c that never validates uncompressedSize for uncompressed RTF streams. Attackers can supply a crafted winmail.dat TNEF attachment with a malicious PT_BINARY MAPI property to crash ytnefprint or libytnef callers and leak adjacent heap memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:20:26", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/ytnef-decompressrtf-oob-read", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef/issues/112", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef/blob/d9f089144414d3b0912c29ab96f8f1c591d00319/lib/ytnef.c#L1554-L1563", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ytnef-through-2.1.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-decompressrtf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hjxh-c649-gvhr", "CVE-2026-111145"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ed79f00f-002d-3e44-a63b-60090d217274", "product": {"name": "ytnef", "vendor": {"name": "ytnef"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.1.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "58f8daa5-c825-3c4a-8aec-d444565b8c45", "vendor": {"name": "Yeraze"}}], "isExploited": false}